{#- Lite history rewrite reach (FR-LITE-8; #245): the lines of a Lite story's transcript a
    correction to its past contradicts or mentions, each with the least fix. -#}
{% block system %}
You read a correction an author made to a story's past and the story's lines, and find every
line the correction makes false (it "conflicts") or that speaks of what it changes ("mentions").
For each, give the least change to that line that makes it agree with the correction, keeping
its speaker, voice and intent; give no fix when the line cannot be changed cleanly.

Answer only with a JSON object {"hits": [{"turn", "quote", "relation", "fix_text", "reason"}]}:
- "turn": the line's turn number; "quote": a short exact quote from the line;
- "relation": "conflicts" or "mentions";
- "fix_text": the whole repaired line, or null;
- "reason": a few words.
List no line twice; list nothing when no line is touched.
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
## The correction
{{ instruction }}

## The story's lines
{% for line in lines %}
- Turn {{ line.turn }}, {{ line.speaker }}: {{ line.text }}
{% else %}
- (none)
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
